const e="gndu-zonal-youth-festival",u=2012,n="Whole 8-page PDF read: the Event Guidelines table (page 1) and the Rules & Regulations (pages 2 to 8). It is the rulebook of the 28th North Zone Inter University Youth Festival held at Guru Nanak Dev University on 7 to 11 November 2012, so the dates are from that past edition and are kept as a Variable only. The document prints no eligibility conditions (age, course, membership), no entry fee, no last date to register, no contact person or phone, no street address, no prizes, points or grades, and no rule for how teams qualify from the Zonal Festival. Where the table and the rules differ the rule text is used and the table is added in the same sentence: Folk Orchestra (rules say up to 12 participants and 7 to 10 minutes, table says 9 participants plus 3 accompanists and 8 to 10 minutes), Skit and Mime (the table lists accompanists, the rules print only the participant limit), Classical Dance (rules say up to 15 minutes including preparation, table says 12 to 15), Group Song (Indian) (setting time 4 minutes, Western 5 minutes). Fine Arts durations: the rules say not more than 2 hours 30 minutes, the table says 120 to 150 minutes. All 25 items of the document are carried by the template.",t={Title:"Rules & Criteria",Subtitle:"Guru Nanak Dev University Zonal Youth Festival. Read the event rules before you register your institution.",NoticeTitle:"Please Read Before Registering",Notice:"Each institution can send only one entry in each item. The rules and time limits below follow the Event Guidelines and Rules & Regulations of the 28th North Zone Inter University Youth Festival ({{FestivalDates}}). The edition printed was hosted at {{Venue}}. Check the dates and venue of your own edition.",Notes:["Each institution can send one entry, team or participant in each item.","Study the rules for each item before you register. The decision of the judges for each event is final and binding on all.","Stage and instrument setting time is counted separately from the performance time. Look at each item for its setting time.","Bring the notes, synopsis or copies the item asks for when you register."],Sections:[{Key:"general",Title:"General Rules",Items:["The items are grouped in five sections: Music, Dance, Literary Events, Theatre and Fine Arts.","Participants must study the rules and regulations of the items they enter.","The decision of the judges appointed for each event is final and binding on all.","Grace time after the end of the allotted time limit is 15 seconds for Light Vocal (Indian), Western Vocal Solo, Elocution, Debate and Mime.","Grace time after the end of the allotted time limit is 30 seconds for all the other items.","The festival is organised under the A.I.U. UNIFESTS scheme of the {{OrganisingBody}}."]},{Key:"eligibility",Title:"Eligibility",Items:["Entries are made by institutions. Each institution can send only one entry in each item.","Each University can send only one Folk Orchestra team.","A Quiz team has three students from one institute.","Elocution has one speaker from each institute.","Debate has two debaters from each institute: one speaks for the motion and the other against it.","Each Fine Arts item has one participant from each institute, except Installation, which has four participants.","The rules do not print an age limit, a course or a membership condition. They do not say whether accompanists must be students."]},{Key:"registration",Title:"How to Register",Items:["Items that need notes, copies or synopses must be handed in at registration. Each item below says what it needs.","Folk/Tribal Dance: send three copies of a brief note on the theme and the text of the song, if any, along with the entry form at registration.","Classical Dance (Indian): send three copies of a brief note on the dance story and the accompanying song with its meaning in Hindi or English at registration.","One Act Play: if the language is a regional one, give the synopsis of the play with an English or Hindi translation to the in-charge of the competition on the day of registration.","Skit: give three copies of the synopsis of the theme, with the language of presentation (Hindi or English), on the day of registration.","The topic of Elocution is announced at the managers' meeting.","The topic of Debate is announced 24 hours in advance.","The sequence of Elocution speakers is decided by a draw of lots.","The rules do not print an entry fee, a last date to register or how to send the entry form."]},{Key:"dates",Title:"Important Dates",Items:["Festival dates in the edition printed: {{FestivalDates}}.","The rules do not print a last date for entries."]},{Key:"venue",Title:"Venue",Items:["The edition printed was hosted at {{Venue}}."]},{Key:"levels",Title:"Zonal and National Festival",Items:["The rules name a Zonal Festival and a National (Inter Zonal) Festival. The speaking time in Elocution and Debate is different at the two levels. It is given in those competitions.","The rules do not say how many teams move up from the Zonal Festival or how they are chosen."]},{Key:"teams",Title:"Entries per Institution",Items:["Each institution can send only one entry in each item.","Group items have a limit on the number of participants and accompanists. The limit is given in each competition.","Accompanists are counted in addition to the participants."]}],Documents:[{Title:"Event Guidelines and Rules & Regulations (PDF)",Url:"https://gndu.ac.in/Events_Rules.pdf"}]},i=[],a=[],s=JSON.parse(`[{"Title":"Classical Vocal Solo","Source":"GNDU Rules & Regulations 1(a); GNDU Event Guidelines at a Glance (page 1)","Sections":{"About":null,"TimeAndFormat":["One participant and up to two accompanists, three people in all.","The duration is 10 minutes. The guideline table gives 8 to 10 minutes.","Stage and instrument setting time is a maximum of 5 minutes."],"Rules":["Only one entry per institution is allowed.","The maximum number of accompanists is two."],"Allowed":["The item can be presented in either Hindustani or Karnatak style."],"NotAllowed":["Cinema songs are not allowed in this item."],"Judging":["Judging is based on tal, selection of raga, composition and general impression."],"Points":null,"Notes":["Take sufficient thought and care when choosing the raga and the composition."]},"Markdown":"## Time and format\\n- One participant and up to two accompanists, three people in all.\\n- The duration is 10 minutes. The guideline table gives 8 to 10 minutes.\\n- Stage and instrument setting time is a maximum of 5 minutes.\\n\\n## Rules\\n- Only one entry per institution is allowed.\\n- The maximum number of accompanists is two.\\n\\n## Allowed\\n- The item can be presented in either Hindustani or Karnatak style.\\n\\n## Not allowed\\n- Cinema songs are not allowed in this item.\\n\\n## Judging\\n- Judging is based on tal, selection of raga, composition and general impression.\\n\\n## Notes for participants\\n- Take sufficient thought and care when choosing the raga and the composition."},{"Title":"Classical Instrumental Solo (Percussion)","Source":"GNDU Rules & Regulations 1(b); GNDU Event Guidelines at a Glance (page 1)","Sections":{"About":null,"TimeAndFormat":["One participant and up to two accompanists, three people in all.","The duration is 10 minutes. The guideline table gives 8 to 10 minutes.","Stage and instrument setting time is a maximum of 5 minutes."],"Rules":["Only one entry per institution is allowed.","The maximum number of accompanists is two.","Participants must bring their own instruments."],"Allowed":["The item can be presented in either Hindustani or Karnatak style."],"NotAllowed":null,"Judging":["Judging is based on tal, selection of raga, composition and general impression."],"Points":null,"Notes":null},"Markdown":"## Time and format\\n- One participant and up to two accompanists, three people in all.\\n- The duration is 10 minutes. The guideline table gives 8 to 10 minutes.\\n- Stage and instrument setting time is a maximum of 5 minutes.\\n\\n## Rules\\n- Only one entry per institution is allowed.\\n- The maximum number of accompanists is two.\\n- Participants must bring their own instruments.\\n\\n## Allowed\\n- The item can be presented in either Hindustani or Karnatak style.\\n\\n## Judging\\n- Judging is based on tal, selection of raga, composition and general impression."},{"Title":"Classical Instrumental Solo (Non-Percussion)","Source":"GNDU Rules & Regulations 1(c); GNDU Event Guidelines at a Glance (page 1)","Sections":{"About":null,"TimeAndFormat":["One participant and up to two accompanists, three people in all.","The duration is 10 minutes. The guideline table gives 8 to 10 minutes.","Stage and instrument setting time is a maximum of 5 minutes."],"Rules":["Only one entry per institution is allowed.","The maximum number of accompanists is two.","Participants must bring their own instruments."],"Allowed":["The item can be presented in either Hindustani or Karnatak style.","Instruments of Western origin that are adapted to the Indian raga system are allowed."],"NotAllowed":["Casio is not allowed."],"Judging":["Judging is based on swara, tal, selection of raga, composition and general impression."],"Points":null,"Notes":null},"Markdown":"## Time and format\\n- One participant and up to two accompanists, three people in all.\\n- The duration is 10 minutes. The guideline table gives 8 to 10 minutes.\\n- Stage and instrument setting time is a maximum of 5 minutes.\\n\\n## Rules\\n- Only one entry per institution is allowed.\\n- The maximum number of accompanists is two.\\n- Participants must bring their own instruments.\\n\\n## Allowed\\n- The item can be presented in either Hindustani or Karnatak style.\\n- Instruments of Western origin that are adapted to the Indian raga system are allowed.\\n\\n## Not allowed\\n- Casio is not allowed.\\n\\n## Judging\\n- Judging is based on swara, tal, selection of raga, composition and general impression."},{"Title":"Light Vocal (Indian)","Source":"GNDU Rules & Regulations 1(d); GNDU Event Guidelines at a Glance (page 1)","Sections":{"About":null,"TimeAndFormat":["One participant and up to two accompanists, three people in all.","The song lasts between 4 and 6 minutes.","Stage and instrument setting time is a maximum of 2 minutes.","Grace time after the time limit is 15 seconds."],"Rules":["Only one entry per institution is allowed.","The number of accompanists must not be more than two."],"Allowed":["Only non-film songs, geet, gazal, bhajan, shabad and abhangas can be presented."],"NotAllowed":null,"Judging":["Judging is based on swara, taal, selection of raga, composition and general impression."],"Points":null,"Notes":null},"Markdown":"## Time and format\\n- One participant and up to two accompanists, three people in all.\\n- The song lasts between 4 and 6 minutes.\\n- Stage and instrument setting time is a maximum of 2 minutes.\\n- Grace time after the time limit is 15 seconds.\\n\\n## Rules\\n- Only one entry per institution is allowed.\\n- The number of accompanists must not be more than two.\\n\\n## Allowed\\n- Only non-film songs, geet, gazal, bhajan, shabad and abhangas can be presented.\\n\\n## Judging\\n- Judging is based on swara, taal, selection of raga, composition and general impression."},{"Title":"Western Vocal Solo","Source":"GNDU Rules & Regulations 1(e); GNDU Event Guidelines at a Glance (page 1)","Sections":{"About":null,"TimeAndFormat":["One participant and up to two accompanists, three people in all.","The song lasts between 4 and 6 minutes.","Stage and instrument setting time is a maximum of 2 minutes.","Grace time after the time limit is 15 seconds."],"Rules":["Only one entry per institution is allowed.","The number of accompanists must not be more than two.","The language of the song must be English only."],"Allowed":null,"NotAllowed":null,"Judging":["Judging is based on composition, rhythm, coordination and general impression."],"Points":null,"Notes":null},"Markdown":"## Time and format\\n- One participant and up to two accompanists, three people in all.\\n- The song lasts between 4 and 6 minutes.\\n- Stage and instrument setting time is a maximum of 2 minutes.\\n- Grace time after the time limit is 15 seconds.\\n\\n## Rules\\n- Only one entry per institution is allowed.\\n- The number of accompanists must not be more than two.\\n- The language of the song must be English only.\\n\\n## Judging\\n- Judging is based on composition, rhythm, coordination and general impression."},{"Title":"Group Song (Western)","Source":"GNDU Rules & Regulations 1(f); GNDU Event Guidelines at a Glance (page 1)","Sections":{"About":null,"TimeAndFormat":["The maximum time for the group song is 10 minutes, not counting setting time. The guideline table gives 8 to 10 minutes.","The setting time for a group must not be more than 5 minutes."],"Rules":["Only one entry per institution is allowed.","A group has a maximum of 6 singers.","The maximum number of accompanists who play instruments is three.","The group songs must be in the English language."],"Allowed":null,"NotAllowed":null,"Judging":["Judging is on the quality of singing only. It is not on make-up, costumes or actions of the team."],"Points":null,"Notes":null},"Markdown":"## Time and format\\n- The maximum time for the group song is 10 minutes, not counting setting time. The guideline table gives 8 to 10 minutes.\\n- The setting time for a group must not be more than 5 minutes.\\n\\n## Rules\\n- Only one entry per institution is allowed.\\n- A group has a maximum of 6 singers.\\n- The maximum number of accompanists who play instruments is three.\\n- The group songs must be in the English language.\\n\\n## Judging\\n- Judging is on the quality of singing only. It is not on make-up, costumes or actions of the team."},{"Title":"Group Song (Indian)","Source":"GNDU Rules & Regulations 1(g); GNDU Event Guidelines at a Glance (page 1)","Sections":{"About":null,"TimeAndFormat":["The maximum time for the group song is 10 minutes, not counting setting time. The guideline table gives 8 to 10 minutes.","The setting time for a group must not be more than 4 minutes."],"Rules":["Only one entry per institution is allowed.","A team presents two songs: one patriotic song and one folk song.","A group has a maximum of 6 singers.","The number of accompanists who play instruments is three.","The group songs must be Indian songs. They can be in a regional language."],"Allowed":null,"NotAllowed":["No film song can be presented as a group song."],"Judging":["Judging is on the quality of singing only. It is not on make-up, costumes or actions of the team."],"Points":null,"Notes":null},"Markdown":"## Time and format\\n- The maximum time for the group song is 10 minutes, not counting setting time. The guideline table gives 8 to 10 minutes.\\n- The setting time for a group must not be more than 4 minutes.\\n\\n## Rules\\n- Only one entry per institution is allowed.\\n- A team presents two songs: one patriotic song and one folk song.\\n- A group has a maximum of 6 singers.\\n- The number of accompanists who play instruments is three.\\n- The group songs must be Indian songs. They can be in a regional language.\\n\\n## Not allowed\\n- No film song can be presented as a group song.\\n\\n## Judging\\n- Judging is on the quality of singing only. It is not on make-up, costumes or actions of the team."},{"Title":"Folk Orchestra","Source":"GNDU Rules & Regulations 1(h); GNDU Event Guidelines at a Glance (page 1)","Sections":{"About":null,"TimeAndFormat":["The performance lasts at least 7 minutes and at most 10 minutes. The guideline table gives 8 to 10 minutes.","Setting time must not be more than 5 minutes."],"Rules":["Each University can send only one team.","The team has up to 12 participants. The guideline table lists 9 participants and 3 accompanists, 12 people in all.","The group can be all boys, all girls or mixed.","Up to three professional accompanists are allowed.","The professional accompanists must wear a different dress from the student participants so that they are easy to identify.","The professional accompanists must sit or stand separately from the participants and must not lead the team."],"Allowed":null,"NotAllowed":null,"Judging":null,"Points":null,"Notes":["The team can present folk tunes that are recognised as folk tunes of the state to which the university belongs, as far as possible."]},"Markdown":"## Time and format\\n- The performance lasts at least 7 minutes and at most 10 minutes. The guideline table gives 8 to 10 minutes.\\n- Setting time must not be more than 5 minutes.\\n\\n## Rules\\n- Each University can send only one team.\\n- The team has up to 12 participants. The guideline table lists 9 participants and 3 accompanists, 12 people in all.\\n- The group can be all boys, all girls or mixed.\\n- Up to three professional accompanists are allowed.\\n- The professional accompanists must wear a different dress from the student participants so that they are easy to identify.\\n- The professional accompanists must sit or stand separately from the participants and must not lead the team.\\n\\n## Notes for participants\\n- The team can present folk tunes that are recognised as folk tunes of the state to which the university belongs, as far as possible."},{"Title":"Folk/Tribal Dance","Source":"GNDU Rules & Regulations 2(a); GNDU Event Guidelines at a Glance (page 1)","Sections":{"About":null,"TimeAndFormat":["The dance lasts not more than 10 minutes. The guideline table gives 8 to 10 minutes.","Time for setting the sets and instruments is a maximum of 5 minutes."],"Rules":["Only one entry per institution is allowed.","A team has a maximum of 10 participants. It can be all boys, all girls or mixed.","The number of accompanists allowed is five.","Three copies of a brief note on the theme and the text of the song, if any, must be given with the entry form at registration.","The team must remove its sets and properties immediately after the performance."],"Allowed":["The dance can be a primitive dance or a folk dance in the Indian style."],"NotAllowed":["A classical dance is not allowed."],"Judging":["Judging is based on rhythm, formation, expression, costumes, make-up, sets and overall effect."],"Points":null,"Notes":null},"Markdown":"## Time and format\\n- The dance lasts not more than 10 minutes. The guideline table gives 8 to 10 minutes.\\n- Time for setting the sets and instruments is a maximum of 5 minutes.\\n\\n## Rules\\n- Only one entry per institution is allowed.\\n- A team has a maximum of 10 participants. It can be all boys, all girls or mixed.\\n- The number of accompanists allowed is five.\\n- Three copies of a brief note on the theme and the text of the song, if any, must be given with the entry form at registration.\\n- The team must remove its sets and properties immediately after the performance.\\n\\n## Allowed\\n- The dance can be a primitive dance or a folk dance in the Indian style.\\n\\n## Not allowed\\n- A classical dance is not allowed.\\n\\n## Judging\\n- Judging is based on rhythm, formation, expression, costumes, make-up, sets and overall effect."},{"Title":"Classical Dance (Indian)","Source":"GNDU Rules & Regulations 2(b); GNDU Event Guidelines at a Glance (page 1)","Sections":{"About":null,"TimeAndFormat":["The participant has up to 15 minutes including time for preparation. The guideline table gives 12 to 15 minutes."],"Rules":["Each institute can send only one entry.","A maximum of three accompanists is allowed.","Three copies of a brief note on the dance story, if any, and on the accompanying song with its meaning in Hindi or English must be given at registration."],"Allowed":["The dance can be from any of the approved schools of dance, such as Kathak, Kathakali, Bharat Natyam, Manipuri, Kuchipudi, Mohiniyattam and Odissi."],"NotAllowed":null,"Judging":["Judging is based on tal, technique, rhythm, abhinaya or expression, costumes, footwork and general impression."],"Points":null,"Notes":null},"Markdown":"## Time and format\\n- The participant has up to 15 minutes including time for preparation. The guideline table gives 12 to 15 minutes.\\n\\n## Rules\\n- Each institute can send only one entry.\\n- A maximum of three accompanists is allowed.\\n- Three copies of a brief note on the dance story, if any, and on the accompanying song with its meaning in Hindi or English must be given at registration.\\n\\n## Allowed\\n- The dance can be from any of the approved schools of dance, such as Kathak, Kathakali, Bharat Natyam, Manipuri, Kuchipudi, Mohiniyattam and Odissi.\\n\\n## Judging\\n- Judging is based on tal, technique, rhythm, abhinaya or expression, costumes, footwork and general impression."},{"Title":"Quiz","Source":"GNDU Rules & Regulations 3(a); GNDU Event Guidelines at a Glance (page 1)","Sections":{"About":null,"TimeAndFormat":null,"Rules":["Each institute can send a team of three students.","There is a written preliminary round. Teams are selected for the final.","The final is oral with audio-visual questions.","The specific rules on how answers are evaluated, the time to reply to a question and the type of round are given before the competition starts."],"Allowed":null,"NotAllowed":null,"Judging":null,"Points":null,"Notes":null},"Markdown":"## Rules\\n- Each institute can send a team of three students.\\n- There is a written preliminary round. Teams are selected for the final.\\n- The final is oral with audio-visual questions.\\n- The specific rules on how answers are evaluated, the time to reply to a question and the type of round are given before the competition starts."},{"Title":"Elocution","Source":"GNDU Rules & Regulations 3(b); GNDU Event Guidelines at a Glance (page 1)","Sections":{"About":null,"TimeAndFormat":["Each speaker can speak for a maximum of 5 minutes at the Zonal Festival and 10 minutes at the National Festival. The guideline table gives 4 to 5 minutes.","Grace time after the time limit is 15 seconds."],"Rules":["Each institute is represented by one speaker.","The medium of expression is Hindi or English.","The performance is judged in one language.","The topic of Elocution is announced at the managers' meeting.","The sequence of speakers is decided by a draw of lots."],"Allowed":["The item can be prose or poetry."],"NotAllowed":["A song is not allowed."],"Judging":null,"Points":null,"Notes":null},"Markdown":"## Time and format\\n- Each speaker can speak for a maximum of 5 minutes at the Zonal Festival and 10 minutes at the National Festival. The guideline table gives 4 to 5 minutes.\\n- Grace time after the time limit is 15 seconds.\\n\\n## Rules\\n- Each institute is represented by one speaker.\\n- The medium of expression is Hindi or English.\\n- The performance is judged in one language.\\n- The topic of Elocution is announced at the managers' meeting.\\n- The sequence of speakers is decided by a draw of lots.\\n\\n## Allowed\\n- The item can be prose or poetry.\\n\\n## Not allowed\\n- A song is not allowed."},{"Title":"Debate","Source":"GNDU Rules & Regulations 3(c); GNDU Event Guidelines at a Glance (page 1)","Sections":{"About":null,"TimeAndFormat":["Each debater can speak for a maximum of 5 minutes at the Zonal Festival and 10 minutes at the National Festival. The guideline table gives 4 to 5 minutes.","Grace time after the time limit is 15 seconds."],"Rules":["Each institute is represented by two debaters. One speaks for the motion and the other speaks against it.","The medium of expression is Hindi or English.","The topic of the debate is announced 24 hours in advance."],"Allowed":null,"NotAllowed":["Paper reading is not allowed."],"Judging":null,"Points":null,"Notes":null},"Markdown":"## Time and format\\n- Each debater can speak for a maximum of 5 minutes at the Zonal Festival and 10 minutes at the National Festival. The guideline table gives 4 to 5 minutes.\\n- Grace time after the time limit is 15 seconds.\\n\\n## Rules\\n- Each institute is represented by two debaters. One speaks for the motion and the other speaks against it.\\n- The medium of expression is Hindi or English.\\n- The topic of the debate is announced 24 hours in advance.\\n\\n## Not allowed\\n- Paper reading is not allowed."},{"Title":"One Act Play","Source":"GNDU Rules & Regulations 4(a); GNDU Event Guidelines at a Glance (page 1)","Sections":{"About":null,"TimeAndFormat":["The play must not be longer than 30 minutes. The guideline table gives 25 to 30 minutes.","Time is counted from the signal or from when the team starts to give an introduction, whichever is earlier.","Empty stage to empty stage must be followed strictly. Up to 10 minutes are given for setting the stage and removing sets and properties after the team takes charge of the stage."],"Rules":["Only one entry is accepted from each institute.","The number of participants must not be more than nine.","The number of accompanists must not be more than three.","The team brings its own set, stage properties and make-up material. Light and general property, such as ordinary furniture, can be provided if the host is told in advance.","Participants can speak in Hindi, English or any regional language of India.","If the language is a regional one, the synopsis of the play with a translation in English or Hindi must be given to the in-charge of the competition on the day of registration.","The team must report to the in-charge of the competition at least two hours before the presentation of the play.","Accompanists speak from the background or play musical instruments for background music."],"Allowed":null,"NotAllowed":["Accompanists must not appear on the stage."],"Judging":["Judging is most likely based on the theme, work on acting, stage craft, design and general impression.","The decision of the panel of judges is final and binding on all."],"Points":null,"Notes":null},"Markdown":"## Time and format\\n- The play must not be longer than 30 minutes. The guideline table gives 25 to 30 minutes.\\n- Time is counted from the signal or from when the team starts to give an introduction, whichever is earlier.\\n- Empty stage to empty stage must be followed strictly. Up to 10 minutes are given for setting the stage and removing sets and properties after the team takes charge of the stage.\\n\\n## Rules\\n- Only one entry is accepted from each institute.\\n- The number of participants must not be more than nine.\\n- The number of accompanists must not be more than three.\\n- The team brings its own set, stage properties and make-up material. Light and general property, such as ordinary furniture, can be provided if the host is told in advance.\\n- Participants can speak in Hindi, English or any regional language of India.\\n- If the language is a regional one, the synopsis of the play with a translation in English or Hindi must be given to the in-charge of the competition on the day of registration.\\n- The team must report to the in-charge of the competition at least two hours before the presentation of the play.\\n- Accompanists speak from the background or play musical instruments for background music.\\n\\n## Not allowed\\n- Accompanists must not appear on the stage.\\n\\n## Judging\\n- Judging is most likely based on the theme, work on acting, stage craft, design and general impression.\\n- The decision of the panel of judges is final and binding on all."},{"Title":"Skit","Source":"GNDU Rules & Regulations 4(b); GNDU Event Guidelines at a Glance (page 1)","Sections":{"About":null,"TimeAndFormat":["The maximum time for each team is 10 minutes. The guideline table gives 8 to 10 minutes."],"Rules":["Only one team per institute is allowed.","A maximum of six participants can take part. The guideline table lists up to three accompanists.","Three copies of the synopsis of the theme, with the language of presentation (Hindi or English), must be given on the day of registration.","Only innocent satire or humour is expected."],"Allowed":["Make-up, drapery and background music are allowed."],"NotAllowed":["Personal remarks, aspersions and character assassination are not allowed.","Vulgarity and bitter insinuations must be avoided."],"Judging":["The item is judged mainly on the theme, work on acting, stage craft, design and general impression."],"Points":null,"Notes":null},"Markdown":"## Time and format\\n- The maximum time for each team is 10 minutes. The guideline table gives 8 to 10 minutes.\\n\\n## Rules\\n- Only one team per institute is allowed.\\n- A maximum of six participants can take part. The guideline table lists up to three accompanists.\\n- Three copies of the synopsis of the theme, with the language of presentation (Hindi or English), must be given on the day of registration.\\n- Only innocent satire or humour is expected.\\n\\n## Allowed\\n- Make-up, drapery and background music are allowed.\\n\\n## Not allowed\\n- Personal remarks, aspersions and character assassination are not allowed.\\n- Vulgarity and bitter insinuations must be avoided.\\n\\n## Judging\\n- The item is judged mainly on the theme, work on acting, stage craft, design and general impression."},{"Title":"Mime","Source":"GNDU Rules & Regulations 4(c); GNDU Event Guidelines at a Glance (page 1)","Sections":{"About":null,"TimeAndFormat":["The performance lasts a maximum of 5 minutes. The guideline table gives 4 to 5 minutes.","Grace time after the time limit is 15 seconds."],"Rules":["Only one entry per institute is accepted.","A maximum of six participants can take part. The guideline table lists up to two accompanists."],"Allowed":null,"NotAllowed":null,"Judging":["Judging is most likely based on the idea, creativity of presentation, use of make-up, music and general impression."],"Points":null,"Notes":null},"Markdown":"## Time and format\\n- The performance lasts a maximum of 5 minutes. The guideline table gives 4 to 5 minutes.\\n- Grace time after the time limit is 15 seconds.\\n\\n## Rules\\n- Only one entry per institute is accepted.\\n- A maximum of six participants can take part. The guideline table lists up to two accompanists.\\n\\n## Judging\\n- Judging is most likely based on the idea, creativity of presentation, use of make-up, music and general impression."},{"Title":"Mimicry","Source":"GNDU Rules & Regulations 4(d); GNDU Event Guidelines at a Glance (page 1)","Sections":{"About":null,"TimeAndFormat":["Each student artist is given 5 minutes at both the Zonal and Inter Zonal Festivals. The guideline table gives 4 to 5 minutes."],"Rules":["Only one entry is allowed."],"Allowed":["Participants can mimic the sound of machines and the speeches of well-known persons, including film personalities."],"NotAllowed":null,"Judging":["Marking is based on skill in imitating, variety of the sounds and voices imitated, and presentation."],"Points":null,"Notes":null},"Markdown":"## Time and format\\n- Each student artist is given 5 minutes at both the Zonal and Inter Zonal Festivals. The guideline table gives 4 to 5 minutes.\\n\\n## Rules\\n- Only one entry is allowed.\\n\\n## Allowed\\n- Participants can mimic the sound of machines and the speeches of well-known persons, including film personalities.\\n\\n## Judging\\n- Marking is based on skill in imitating, variety of the sounds and voices imitated, and presentation."},{"Title":"On the Spot Painting","Source":"GNDU Rules & Regulations 5(a); GNDU Event Guidelines at a Glance (page 1)","Sections":{"About":null,"TimeAndFormat":["The duration is not more than 2 hours 30 minutes. The guideline table gives 120 to 150 minutes."],"Rules":["The painting is done on the subject given by the in-charge of the competition.","The size of the painting is half imperial size drawing paper, that is 22 inches x 15 inches.","Candidates bring their own material such as brushes and paints. Only the paper or sheet is provided by the host institute."],"Allowed":["The painting can be done in oil, water, poster or pastel colours."],"NotAllowed":null,"Judging":null,"Points":null,"Notes":null},"Markdown":"## Time and format\\n- The duration is not more than 2 hours 30 minutes. The guideline table gives 120 to 150 minutes.\\n\\n## Rules\\n- The painting is done on the subject given by the in-charge of the competition.\\n- The size of the painting is half imperial size drawing paper, that is 22 inches x 15 inches.\\n- Candidates bring their own material such as brushes and paints. Only the paper or sheet is provided by the host institute.\\n\\n## Allowed\\n- The painting can be done in oil, water, poster or pastel colours."},{"Title":"Collage","Source":"GNDU Rules & Regulations 5(b); GNDU Event Guidelines at a Glance (page 1)","Sections":{"About":null,"TimeAndFormat":["The duration is not more than 2 hours 30 minutes. The guideline table gives 120 to 150 minutes."],"Rules":["The collage is made on the given topic or subject on a sheet of 15 inches x 22 inches.","Participants bring their own scissors, paste and other material.","The host university provides the drawing paper of 22 inches x 15 inches.","The collage must be made from old magazines."],"Allowed":null,"NotAllowed":null,"Judging":null,"Points":null,"Notes":null},"Markdown":"## Time and format\\n- The duration is not more than 2 hours 30 minutes. The guideline table gives 120 to 150 minutes.\\n\\n## Rules\\n- The collage is made on the given topic or subject on a sheet of 15 inches x 22 inches.\\n- Participants bring their own scissors, paste and other material.\\n- The host university provides the drawing paper of 22 inches x 15 inches.\\n- The collage must be made from old magazines."},{"Title":"Poster Making","Source":"GNDU Rules & Regulations 5(c); GNDU Event Guidelines at a Glance (page 1)","Sections":{"About":null,"TimeAndFormat":["The duration is not more than 2 hours 30 minutes. The guideline table gives 120 to 150 minutes."],"Rules":["The poster is made on the subject, topic or theme given by the in-charge of the competition.","Participants bring their own material. Only the drawing paper or sheet of 22 inches x 15 inches is provided by the organisers."],"Allowed":null,"NotAllowed":null,"Judging":null,"Points":null,"Notes":null},"Markdown":"## Time and format\\n- The duration is not more than 2 hours 30 minutes. The guideline table gives 120 to 150 minutes.\\n\\n## Rules\\n- The poster is made on the subject, topic or theme given by the in-charge of the competition.\\n- Participants bring their own material. Only the drawing paper or sheet of 22 inches x 15 inches is provided by the organisers."},{"Title":"Clay Modeling","Source":"GNDU Rules & Regulations 5(d); GNDU Event Guidelines at a Glance (page 1)","Sections":{"About":null,"TimeAndFormat":["The duration is not more than 2 hours 30 minutes. The guideline table gives 120 to 150 minutes."],"Rules":["The topics, size and other specific rules are announced on the spot.","The clay is provided by the host institute."],"Allowed":null,"NotAllowed":null,"Judging":null,"Points":null,"Notes":null},"Markdown":"## Time and format\\n- The duration is not more than 2 hours 30 minutes. The guideline table gives 120 to 150 minutes.\\n\\n## Rules\\n- The topics, size and other specific rules are announced on the spot.\\n- The clay is provided by the host institute."},{"Title":"Cartooning","Source":"GNDU Rules & Regulations 5(e); GNDU Event Guidelines at a Glance (page 1)","Sections":{"About":null,"TimeAndFormat":["The duration is not more than 2 hours 30 minutes. The guideline table gives 120 to 150 minutes."],"Rules":["The cartoon is made on the given subject or idea.","Participants bring their own material. Only the drawing paper of 22 inches x 15 inches is provided by the host institute."],"Allowed":null,"NotAllowed":null,"Judging":null,"Points":null,"Notes":null},"Markdown":"## Time and format\\n- The duration is not more than 2 hours 30 minutes. The guideline table gives 120 to 150 minutes.\\n\\n## Rules\\n- The cartoon is made on the given subject or idea.\\n- Participants bring their own material. Only the drawing paper of 22 inches x 15 inches is provided by the host institute."},{"Title":"Rangoli","Source":"GNDU Rules & Regulations 5(f); GNDU Event Guidelines at a Glance (page 1)","Sections":{"About":null,"TimeAndFormat":["The duration is not more than 2 hours 30 minutes. The guideline table gives 120 to 150 minutes."],"Rules":["Participants bring their own material.","This art is known by different names in various regions, such as Mandna, Alpana, Alekhan, Kolam and Rangoli. The medium and form of expression can be free hand, pictorial and descriptive.","Only one medium can be used: poster colours, flower petals, saw-dust, pulses or rice, without pasting.","Participants must prepare the rangoli within the space provided by the organisers."],"Allowed":null,"NotAllowed":null,"Judging":null,"Points":null,"Notes":null},"Markdown":"## Time and format\\n- The duration is not more than 2 hours 30 minutes. The guideline table gives 120 to 150 minutes.\\n\\n## Rules\\n- Participants bring their own material.\\n- This art is known by different names in various regions, such as Mandna, Alpana, Alekhan, Kolam and Rangoli. The medium and form of expression can be free hand, pictorial and descriptive.\\n- Only one medium can be used: poster colours, flower petals, saw-dust, pulses or rice, without pasting.\\n- Participants must prepare the rangoli within the space provided by the organisers."},{"Title":"Spot Photography","Source":"GNDU Rules & Regulations 5(g); GNDU Event Guidelines at a Glance (page 1)","Sections":{"About":null,"TimeAndFormat":["The time limit is 2 hours 30 minutes. The guideline table gives 120 to 150 minutes."],"Rules":["Each institution can send one participant.","The participant brings his or her own digital camera of not more than 12 megapixels.","The camera must have a memory card. The judges format the memory card before the contest starts.","The participant captures 5 photographs on the theme announced on the spot by the judges.","The organisers have all rights to use the pictures as and when they decide.","Additional instructions are announced on the spot."],"Allowed":null,"NotAllowed":["No mixing, matching or morphing of photographs is allowed.","Software such as Photoshop for enhancing images is not allowed."],"Judging":["Digital images are evaluated on impact, composition, technical quality and suitability for the theme."],"Points":null,"Notes":null},"Markdown":"## Time and format\\n- The time limit is 2 hours 30 minutes. The guideline table gives 120 to 150 minutes.\\n\\n## Rules\\n- Each institution can send one participant.\\n- The participant brings his or her own digital camera of not more than 12 megapixels.\\n- The camera must have a memory card. The judges format the memory card before the contest starts.\\n- The participant captures 5 photographs on the theme announced on the spot by the judges.\\n- The organisers have all rights to use the pictures as and when they decide.\\n- Additional instructions are announced on the spot.\\n\\n## Not allowed\\n- No mixing, matching or morphing of photographs is allowed.\\n- Software such as Photoshop for enhancing images is not allowed.\\n\\n## Judging\\n- Digital images are evaluated on impact, composition, technical quality and suitability for the theme."},{"Title":"Installation","Source":"GNDU Rules & Regulations 5(h); GNDU Event Guidelines at a Glance (page 1)","Sections":{"About":["Install or create an atmosphere related to the subject or title of the installation."],"TimeAndFormat":["The duration is not more than 2 hours 30 minutes. The guideline table gives 120 to 150 minutes."],"Rules":["This is a group activity. Four participants take part but they create only one installation.","The size of the installation must not be bigger than 5 feet x 5 feet x 5 feet."],"Allowed":["Participants can use all the material used in other art items such as cartooning, painting, rangoli, poster, collage and clay modeling.","Participants can use waste material that is available in the surroundings, or take any material from outside."],"NotAllowed":["Already composed images or forms available in the market cannot be used. Participants must compose or create their own image from raw material."],"Judging":null,"Points":null,"Notes":null},"Markdown":"## About this competition\\n- Install or create an atmosphere related to the subject or title of the installation.\\n\\n## Time and format\\n- The duration is not more than 2 hours 30 minutes. The guideline table gives 120 to 150 minutes.\\n\\n## Rules\\n- This is a group activity. Four participants take part but they create only one installation.\\n- The size of the installation must not be bigger than 5 feet x 5 feet x 5 feet.\\n\\n## Allowed\\n- Participants can use all the material used in other art items such as cartooning, painting, rangoli, poster, collage and clay modeling.\\n- Participants can use waste material that is available in the surroundings, or take any material from outside.\\n\\n## Not allowed\\n- Already composed images or forms available in the market cannot be used. Participants must compose or create their own image from raw material."}]`),o=[],l=[{Key:"FestivalDates",Kind:"date",Label:"Festival dates",Value:"7 to 11 November 2012 (28th North Zone Inter University Youth Festival, the edition printed)",Source:"GNDU Event Guidelines at a Glance (page 1), cover"},{Key:"Venue",Kind:"address",Label:"Festival host and venue",Value:{Name:"Guru Nanak Dev University",Address:"",City:"Amritsar",MapUrl:"",Directions:""},Source:"GNDU Event Guidelines at a Glance (page 1), cover. The document prints no street address."},{Key:"OrganisingBody",Kind:"text",Label:"Organising body",Value:"Ministry of Youth Affairs & Sports, Government of India (A.I.U. UNIFESTS)",Source:"GNDU Event Guidelines at a Glance (page 1), cover"}],r=[{Claim:"All rules, time limits, participant and accompanist numbers, setting times, judging criteria and registration notes captured from the host university's own 'Event Guidelines at a Glance' table and 'Rules & Regulations' for 25 items in five sections.",SourceType:"Primary - organiser's own rules",Source:"GNDU Events_Rules.pdf, 28th North Zone Inter University Youth Festival",Url:"https://gndu.ac.in/Events_Rules.pdf"}],m={TemplateKey:e,Year:2012,Note:n,Page:t,ParticipantTypes:i,AgeGroups:a,Competitions:s,CompetitionAgeGroups:o,Variables:l,Evidence:r};export{a as AgeGroups,o as CompetitionAgeGroups,s as Competitions,r as Evidence,n as Note,t as Page,i as ParticipantTypes,e as TemplateKey,l as Variables,u as Year,m as default};
